#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eacccd2-6f0b-56a0-af15-03a8df8a4aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431680} {:answer/id #uuid "5df049c4-9c88-5398-9a72-6c30494cabef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431682} {:answer/id #uuid "80ce9f4b-db00-53a4-9818-0baaa275e656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431683} {:answer/id #uuid "aed23c8f-009b-55ee-8619-d778834839e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431687} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ebdc55-f316-53b9-bb25-7a4ac5579ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80ce9f4b-db00-53a4-9818-0baaa275e656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431683} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b76e06b-b313-5d59-b449-7b9e393426a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5536a355-6822-5a47-a0a6-be384dfb79e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126432" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $A(2,-3,5)$ and $B(3,1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $A$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=a+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $a$ is the position vector of $A.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $A(2,-3,5)$ and $B(3,1,-2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105898 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1339a533-dfd9-5aa8-8328-6269486f9c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,3,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,4,-5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431675} {:answer/id #uuid "38ce3564-96d6-5aa9-8f31-aca072b73313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(3,2,1)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,5,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431676} {:answer/id #uuid "9124bc93-158c-5515-bd32-81970e107298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,4,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431684} {:answer/id #uuid "cfbd0720-72fa-5325-aa30-34ea538948f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,3,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431693} {:answer/id #uuid "e55a4e80-0a0f-5330-8c1a-123763b280cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,-2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,4,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9124bc93-158c-5515-bd32-81970e107298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,4,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431684} :answer-field/id #uuid "9028126a-fede-53d4-8337-146b30a620e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "194bde74-7427-5189-95d5-f403b6acd3c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-126965" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,3,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-4,-2,4⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨-4,-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨-4,-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨-4,-2,4⟩)-⟨3,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-4,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t,\\,-2t,\\,4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=3,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =3 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =3 \\\\ |⟨-4t,\\,-2t,\\,4t⟩| & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{(-4t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+(4t)^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{36{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\pm 6t & =3 \\\\ t & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,3,1⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨-4,-2,4⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,3,1⟩-\\frac{1}{2}⟨-4,-2,4⟩=⟨5,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,4,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ac29229-afea-5c3b-9d80-98e4c4817571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431678} {:answer/id #uuid "9cebf039-4878-51b4-a3a9-d495dbdcdfb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431686} {:answer/id #uuid "c99bd56d-b16e-5836-93b7-59a7d5bea293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431692} {:answer/id #uuid "d760676b-c91b-55f6-95ef-1e2c1a8316a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431694} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd0ca81-588c-520c-9d6e-ae9aea95547e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d760676b-c91b-55f6-95ef-1e2c1a8316a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431694} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f5ad19-8ad8-5ef4-8b4d-3a3b41390749" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09c49afc-6085-50e6-863a-8dee0d62b478" :question/math-academy-id "q-162163" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-1,2,-3)$ and $Q(-2,0,4).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ a \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+7+0=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a5c39e-5d72-5455-aec8-eb86a65caf2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431681} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d5149a-691b-58ab-8849-b5bdde35f7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431688} {:answer/id #uuid "b4067977-bbce-543b-8574-d1b46a630254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431689} {:answer/id #uuid "dd35f8ed-d92f-5862-8188-f38211a0649f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431695} {:answer/id #uuid "ebce683f-51aa-5b02-8297-81246cd6de01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4067977-bbce-543b-8574-d1b46a630254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431689} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb53027-c7e0-55e6-85b6-4d8da4b5b3e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf9c9d04-5ab5-558b-bf38-eae2eb3b3fea" :question/math-academy-id "q-35972" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $M(-1,-2,-3)$ and $N(2,3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $M$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=m+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $m$ is the position vector of $M.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $M(-1,-2,-3)$ and $N(2,3,4)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{MN} \\\\  & =⟨2,3,4⟩-⟨-1,-2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105898 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "416c72c0-8fb5-5d68-8b29-8af5bf68ead0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(14,7,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-1,-5,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431677} {:answer/id #uuid "4af680d4-f96a-54d6-a42c-84ed0f82803b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(7,12,2)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-10,-1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431679} {:answer/id #uuid "992d7033-f50d-5a79-9ab6-cbf67a0e1e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(7,14,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-1,-10,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431685} {:answer/id #uuid "c5acab05-2c88-5065-9ff0-9e18e32d1ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(7,14,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-5,-1,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431690} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c7a32e-0763-553a-ae8f-36a7709abe9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(7,12,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-1,-5,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992d7033-f50d-5a79-9ab6-cbf67a0e1e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Y}_{1}(7,14,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-1,-10,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431685} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4fda4c-a5fe-531d-a4cc-08d2ea5d8a53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c91c661d-e879-5f90-a5fb-ceb93bf19954" :question/math-academy-id "q-69807" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,2,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.$ Find all the possible points $Y$ on that line such that $YP=\\sqrt{160}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩+t⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Y$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OY} & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩+t⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PY} & =\\overset{\\to }{OY}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩+t⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩)-⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =t⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,3t,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PY=\\sqrt{160},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}YP & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PY}| & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,3t,\\,0⟩| & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(3t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\ \\pm \\sqrt{10}t & =4\\sqrt{10} \\\\ t & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 4$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Y}_{1}}=⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩+4⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩=⟨7,14,1⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Y}_{2}}=⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩-4⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩=⟨-1,-10,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Y}_{1}(7,14,1)$ and ${Y}_{2}(-1,-10,1).$"}]}
